STILL DISCLOSED, not defects in this build:
  - THE RULE AND ITS THRESHOLD, stated: a non-zero percentage that would
  -    render as all zeros at the precision in force renders as less-than
  -    the smallest magnitude that precision can show -- <0.1% at one
  -    decimal, <0.01% at two -- and a negative mirrors to >-0.1%. The
  -    threshold is 10 to the minus decimals, derived from the precision
  -    the rule already declares, so it is not a constant that can drift.
  -    A TRUE zero is left alone, because it really is absent.
  - THE RENDER FIX IS SAFE ONLY BECAUSE OF ITS BASELINE. Applying the row
  -    rules on the page without the kept-figure baseline republishes 47 of
  -    the payload 49 declared cells -- D2/2023 would put
  -    0.32057920404599916 over a filed 0.321 and D4/2024 would overwrite a
  -    filed 0.4 with 0.3397. The stored rows are passed as that baseline
  -    and 0 move. The suite drives both callings and requires the
  -    difference.
  - A RECORDED DECISION WAS SUPERSEDED, not quietly reversed. CLCPA-270
  -    deliberately left these rows typeable because their denominator was
  -    not in the table and the preparer had to file them. CLCPA-308 then
  -    declared them, so the engine fills them from rows that ARE in the
  -    table: the premise changed, not the judgement.
  - WHAT THIS WAVE DOES NOT TOUCH: the Section F board. CLCPA-312 is parked
